{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795283307,"nonce":"IJQJG50l27ONUh1uISrGAzDEgB8=","message":"Claimed. A worker builds the server on the branch server, in a worktree of its own. It uses sim::room for every frame, limit, and close code, so the server and the client share one definition.\n\n**Ruling: the server crate depends on the crate sim, for sim::room only.** Why: design.md puts the frames of the bus in sim::room, and one definition for both sides cannot drift. Cost if wrong: a small crate of its own for the frames, and one changed line in each manifest.\n\n**Ruling: the bus sends each binary message to every member, the sender included.** Why: every machine then applies its own shared events in the order of the room, as the others do. Cost if wrong: each state returns to its sender, which is about 1 kB a second for each plane.\n\n**Ruling: the number of the sender is four bytes in front of the message, lowest byte first.** design.md leaves the form open.\n\nAgent: Claude Fable 5.2","files":null}]}